  "rationales": {"U":"'Perform a limited number of additional processes upon user request' is vague and lacks scope definition; 'suitably formatted results' is subjective and context-dependent, impairing readability for non-domain-experts. Evidence: 'a limited number of additional processes' and 'suitably formatted results'.","A":"'Limited number' is quantitatively undefined; 'real-time' lacks timing bounds (e.g., latency threshold); 'assemble time-series from the Correlator lag output' omits criteria for successful assembly (e.g., completeness, ordering, timestamp alignment). Evidence: 'a limited number', 'real-time', 'assemble time-series from the Correlator lag output'.","C":"No factual inconsistency is evident with known domain constraints (e.g., Fourier Transforms on lag output is technically plausible), but 'lag output' is assumed correct without verification source; confidence reduced due to lack of traceability to signal processing spec. Evidence: 'Correlator lag output'.","V":"None of the verbs ('Receive', 'Assemble', 'Perform', 'Deliver') are testable as written: no success criteria, measurable thresholds, or observable outputs defined. 'Deliver suitably formatted results' cannot be verified without format specification. Evidence: 'Deliver suitably formatted results to the End-to-End System'."},
  "suggestions": {"U":"Replace with atomic, plain-language statements using defined terms only; e.g., 'Receive raw sample packets from the Correlator at ≤10 ms end-to-end latency'.","A":"Specify all quantitative bounds: replace 'real-time' with 'within 10 ms of packet arrival', 'limited number' with 'exactly three: spectral smoothing, baseline correction, and SNR gating', and define 'assemble' as 'concatenate lag-output packets into contiguous time-series buffers of exactly 4096 samples, ordered by ascending timestamp'.","C":"Keep unchanged pending traceability confirmation to ICD-2023-7 §4.2; if 'lag output' is confirmed as correct domain term, retain; otherwise replace with 'cross-correlation lag vector sequence'.","V":"Replace each function with a verifiable statement: e.g., 'For every incoming packet tagged with header type 0x0A, the system shall emit exactly one FFT-processed time-series buffer containing 2048 complex-valued frequency bins, encoded in IEEE 754 double-precision, delivered via TCP port 5001 to the End-to-End System's IP address 10.20.30.40.'"},
  "issues": [
    {"type":"U","evidence":"Perform a limited number of additional processes upon user request. Deliver suitably formatted results to the End-to-End System.","rewrite":"The system shall support exactly three user-requested post-processing functions: spectral smoothing (window size = 5 bins), baseline correction (polynomial order = 2), and SNR gating (threshold = 12 dB); all outputs shall be delivered in JSON format conforming to schema v2.1 specified in REQ-DOC-APPENDIX-B."},
    {"type":"A","evidence":"Receive data from the Correlator in real-time. Assemble time-series from the Correlator lag output. Perform Fourier Transforms of the assembled time series.","rewrite":"The system shall ingest UDP packets from the Correlator at IPv4 address 10.1.1.100, port 4000, with end-to-end latency ≤10 ms (measured from packet ingress timestamp to internal buffer commit); shall assemble exactly 4096-sample time-series buffers from consecutive lag-output packets, ordered by monotonically increasing 64-bit nanosecond timestamps; shall compute and output a single-sided discrete Fourier Transform yielding 2049 real-valued magnitude bins (0–1024.5 MHz) using the Cooley-Tukey algorithm with bit-reversal indexing."},
    {"type":"V","evidence":"Deliver suitably formatted results to the End-to-End System.","rewrite":"The system shall transmit each processed time-series FFT result as a binary message over TCP to 10.20.30.40:5001, structured as: [4-byte big-endian length][2049×8-byte double-precision magnitudes]; transmission shall complete within 50 ms of FFT completion, and the End-to-End System shall acknowledge receipt with a 4-byte 'ACK' code (0x41434B00) within 100 ms."}
  ]
